{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/67yvyp","slide":2,"text":"The core idea is simple: take a 30-second segment of single-channel EEG, learn its time-frequency patterns, and predict one of five sleep stages.\nThe project objectives are to build the pipeline, compare model components, and evaluate generalization to unseen subjects.\n[Sources]\n- https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-026-62832-5\n- https://physionet.org/content/sleep-edfx/1.0.0/"}
